+# q, k, v and the output gate are GPTQ in act order over the fwht128-rotated weight, coded by a
+# computed 2^16-state trellis down each column under one f32 scale a row (IQR-V4, docs/IQR.md); the
+# output projection takes a bf16 scale a (row, 128); the lm_head is int8 by round to nearest.
+# inkling2loop serves them at i8a8h behind had_quant_act_i8g. The experts keep the release's NVFP4
+# and MXFP8; the relative-position projection, sink, taps and message gates stay bf16. Every one of
+# these GEMMs gives a token the same bytes at any row count, so greedy output is the same with
+# speculation on and off; an int8 relative projection (the int8 narrow tile) would not.
+#
+# CALIB holds the RADGRAM2 files of an inkling2loop calibration run over a bf16 container
+# (docs/TOOLS.md, "The calibration mode"); each looped layer's Hessian sums its three passes.
+#
+#   CALIB=<Hessians> rad-convert <Inkling-2-Mini> --recipe data/recipes/inkling2-mini-iqr5.recipe \
